# route: level=w3_l2_coop difficulty=beginner players=2 ends=exit after=tally expect=eggs:0,wipes:0,x2_gates:2,painting:26,min_checkpoints:3
# The Beginner two-stream route of Crystal Grotto in co-op (designer DB3; P1|P2, keys L R U D F K S; recorded from
# closed-loop duo macros with a hurt-driven repair search, build/db3/bot_w3_l2_coop.gd). P1 baits the first
# Shellback in front while P2 jumps over it and clubs its back; P1 leads through the gallery, P2 replays his moves a
# little later; P1 picks up the swirling axe. At the leaper lake P1 curls up at the near lip (Down + Swap: a curl,
# never a swap in co-op) and P2 bats him over the icy pool with the club (gate 'drive'); P1 strikes the far drum, P2
# the near one on the count of three: the floes freeze into a bridge and P2 walks over (gate 'floes'). Below, both
# bounce on the Raptor until the twin leapers are down and jump the ice pits; up the crystal shaft one slab apart;
# in the skylight cave P2 Shoulder-Hops off P1's head onto the crystal cache for Cave Painting 26 (not the warp) and
# both walk into the exit (the team exit). Nobody stands 243 ticks without input.
# Re-recorded in wf10 by party with DB3's bot and its hurt-driven repair search (downs only, 36 attempts, fixes in
# build/party11): G54 - a head is never a step into rock - refuses the Totem Ride that lifted P1 into the gallery's roof at
# tick 1105 of the old recording, so the lower gallery plays out differently; 1628 ticks.
